        </relations>
    </header>
    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="33" relname="background">One of the links on our HCI website was to Vincent Flanders Web Pages that Suck.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="34" relname="span">The name of the site sort of jumped out at me</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="35" relname="span">and I thought it would be more of a joke than anything else.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="3" relname="elaboration">The site has a look and feel that is hard to take serious;</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="33" relname="span">however, I found that it contained a lot of useful web design information.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="49" relname="span">The following are some web design concepts I found under the section titled The Biggest Web Design Mistakes of 2004.</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="51" relname="preparation">Vincent Flanders wrote,</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="51" relname="span">Write these two sentences where you can see them as you're working on your computer:</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="52" relname="list">1. The only reason my web site exists is to solve my customers' problems.</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="52" relname="list">2. What problems does the page I'm looking at solve?</segment>
        <segment id="11" parent="53" relname="span">You should be able to look at the home page of any site and figure out what the site is about within four seconds.</segment>
        <segment id="12" parent="11" relname="otherwise">If you can't, your site has failed.</segment>
        <segment id="13" parent="54" relname="span">All web navigation must answer:</segment>
        <segment id="14" parent="48" relname="list">Where am I?</segment>
        <segment id="15" parent="48" relname="list">Where have I been?</segment>
        <segment id="16" parent="48" relname="list">Where can I go next</segment>
        <segment id="17" parent="48" relname="list">Where's the Home Page</segment>
        <segment id="18" parent="48" relname="list">Where's the Home Page</segment>
        <segment id="19" parent="45" relname="concession">Yes, it's called a web page,</segment>
        <segment id="20" parent="45" relname="span">but that doesn't mean you have to cram all your material on one page.</segment>
        <segment id="21" parent="20" relname="volitional-cause">Most folks don't like to scroll.</segment>
        <segment id="22" parent="38" relname="volitional-cause">It's very easy to keep adding material to your home page</segment>
        <segment id="23" parent="39" relname="span">until it gets out of control.</segment>
        <segment id="24" parent="43" relname="span">Smaller business sites are especially susceptible</segment>
        <segment id="25" parent="24" relname="volitional-cause">because they fear they'll miss a sale.</segment>
        <segment id="26" parent="40" relname="span">With so much content vying for attention its initially impossible for the eye to settle on one thing.</segment>
        <segment id="27" parent="41" relname="conjunction">People get confused</segment>
        <segment id="28" parent="41" relname="conjunction">and people leave.</segment>
        <segment id="29" parent="42" relname="span">Pages with lots of disparate material means you have failed to organize your site properly</segment>
        <segment id="30" parent="29" relname="volitional-result">-- probably a combination of not planning your site and poor navigation.</segment>
        <group id="31" type="span"/>
        <group id="32" type="span" parent="31" relname="span"/>
        <group id="33" type="span" parent="56" relname="span"/>
